From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:32:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] egl/android: advertise EXT_pixel_format_float only with a
 float config

The DRI2 display advertises EGL_EXT_pixel_format_float on every
platform, but the Android visuals are all fixed-point, so an Android
display never has a float config. The framework's HWUI takes the
extension as the promise of a half-float window config: each process
that starts a renderer asks for one, finds none, and logs "Device claims
wide gamut support, cannot find matching config". Advertise the
extension on Android only when the visuals produced a float config.
EGL_COLOR_COMPONENT_TYPE_EXT stays queryable, so the platform loader
still reads each config's component type.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c
index f80484fcd0b37ceab33fe077564ecba3edb4ee6d..a6e1bef3aa0d1e9f34c3e7bba0890972668a205f 100644
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_android.c
@@ -865,6 +865,20 @@ droid_add_configs_for_visuals(_EGLDisplay *disp)
    }
 }
 
+/* Whether any config the Android visuals produced renders to float
+ * components.
+ */
+static EGLBoolean
+droid_has_float_config(_EGLDisplay *disp)
+{
+   for (EGLint i = 0; disp->Configs && i < disp->Configs->Size; i++) {
+      const _EGLConfig *conf = disp->Configs->Elements[i];
+      if (conf->ComponentType == EGL_COLOR_COMPONENT_TYPE_FLOAT_EXT)
+         return EGL_TRUE;
+   }
+   return EGL_FALSE;
+}
+
 static const struct dri2_egl_display_vtbl droid_display_vtbl = {
    .authenticate = NULL,
    .create_window_surface = droid_create_window_surface,
@@ -1288,6 +1302,13 @@ dri2_initialize_android(_EGLDisplay *disp)
     */
    droid_add_configs_for_visuals(disp);
 
+   /* The framework's HWUI reads EGL_EXT_pixel_format_float as the promise of
+    * a half-float window config and logs an error in every process that
+    * starts a renderer when there is none. Every visual above is fixed-point,
+    * so advertise the extension only if a float config was added anyway.
+    */
+   disp->Extensions.EXT_pixel_format_float = droid_has_float_config(disp);
+
    /* Fill vtbl last to prevent accidentally calling virtual function during
     * initialization.
     */
